        unescoIntangible=['Traditional music of the Morin Khuur', 'Urtiin Duu, traditional folk long song', 'Naadam, Mongolian traditional festival', 'Mongolian traditional art of Khöömei (throat singing)', 'Falconry, a living human heritage', 'Traditional craftsmanship of the Mongol Ger and associated customs', 'Mongolian calligraphy'],
        famousPeople=['Genghis Khan', 'Kublai Khan', 'Hakuho Sho (Münkhbatyn Davaajargal - greatest sumo Yokozuna in history)', 'The HU (global rock band)', 'Naidangiin Tüvshinbayar (first Olympic Gold medalist)', 'Zanabazar', 'Ukhnaagiin Khürelsükh', 'Luvsannamsrain Oyun-Erdene'],
        flagDescription='Three equal vertical bands of red (hoist, symbolizing progress and prosperity), blue (middle, symbolizing the eternal blue sky), and red (fly); centered on the hoist-side red band is the golden national emblem of Mongolia, the Soyombo (an ancient geometric ideogram representing fire, sun, moon, two fish, two triangles, and two vertical bars symbolizing national freedom and sovereignty).',
        coatOfArmsDescription='A circular blue emblem featuring the Wind Horse (Khiimori) galloping within the Soyombo ideogram, bordered by a continuous swastika-patterned wheel of eternity, surmounted by the Three Jewels (Cintamani), backed by a lotus base and flanked by a traditional green scarf (Khadag).',
        symbols={'animal': 'Przewalski\'s horse (Takhi) and Snow leopard (Irves)', 'bird': 'Saker falcon (Falco cherrug)', 'tree': 'Siberian larch (Larix sibirica)', 'flower': 'Scabiosa comosa (Pasture scabious)'},
        landmarks=['Genghis Khan Equestrian Statue at Tsonjin Boldog (giant 40m stainless steel monument)', 'Erdene Zuu Monastery (Karakorum)', 'Lake Khövsgöl (The Dark Blue Pearl)', 'Flaming Cliffs (Bayanzag in the Gobi Desert - where Roy Chapman Andrews discovered the first dinosaur eggs in 1923)', 'Khustain Nuruu National Park (wild Takhi horses)', 'Amarbayasgalant Monastery', 'Sükhbaatar / Genghis Khan Square (Ulaanbaatar)', 'Khongoryn Els (Singing Sand Dunes)'],
        travelNotes='Visa-free entry for citizens of over 60 countries under the "Visit Mongolia" national initiative; summer months (June to August) offer glorious sunny weather, green steppe landscapes, and the Naadam Festival; winter travel offers dramatic frozen landscapes and eagle hunting festivals but requires heavy sub-zero thermal gear; cash (Tögrög) and local cards are widely used in Ulaanbaatar, while cash is essential in rural aimags.',
        shortSummary='Mongolia is the legendary Land of the Eternal Blue Sky, an epic Eurasian steppe nation celebrated for the world-conquering history of Genghis Khan, the pristine alpine jewel of Lake Khövsgöl, timeless nomadic horse-herding traditions, and the haunting beauty of throat singing and the horsehead fiddle.'
