        unescoIntangible=['Tentative listings: Traditional craftsmanship of Newar metal casting, Lok Dohori folk singing, Dashain cultural festival'],
        famousPeople=['Gautama Buddha', 'Tenzing Norgay', 'Laxmi Prasad Devkota', 'Bhanubhakta Acharya', 'Nirmal Purja (Nimsdai)', 'Mira Rai', 'K.P. Sharma Oli', 'Rohit Paudel (cricket captain)', 'Araniko'],
        flagDescription='The world\'s only non-quadrilateral national flag: a combination of two vertical red triangular pennants bordered in deep blue; the upper pennant bears a white stylized crescent moon with eight rays, and the lower pennant bears a white twelve-pointed sun (symbolizing the desire for the nation to endure as long as the sun and moon).',
        coatOfArmsDescription='A circular emblem depicting Mount Everest in the background, a white map of Nepal on green hills, joined male and female hands symbolizing gender equality, framed by sheaves of rice and a garland of red rhododendrons, topped by the national flag, inscribed below with the national motto "Mother and Motherland Are Greater Than Heaven".',
        symbols={'animal': 'Cow (sacred national animal / Gai)', 'bird': 'Himalayan monal (Danphe - iridescent rainbow pheasant)', 'tree': 'Rhododendron arboreum (Lali Gurans)', 'flower': 'Rhododendron (Lali Gurans - blooming brilliantly across spring hills)'},
        landmarks=['Mount Everest / Sagarmatha Base Camp', 'Boudhanath Stupa (giant mandala stupa in Kathmandu)', 'Pashupatinath Temple (sacred Hindu temple on the Bagmati River)', 'Bhaktapur Durbar Square and Nyatapola Temple', 'Swayambhunath (The Monkey Temple)', 'Phewa Lake and Peace Pagoda (Pokhara)', 'Lumbini Sacred Garden and Maya Devi Temple', 'Chitwan National Park (rhino and tiger safari)', 'Annapurna Sanctuary'],
        travelNotes='Extremely welcoming, peaceful, and tourist-friendly country; tourist visas available on arrival at Kathmandu airport and land borders; autumn (September to November) and spring (March to May) offer the clearest mountain views and ideal trekking conditions; domestic flights to remote mountain airstrips (like Lukla) depend on weather; always register for the Trekkers\' Information Management System (TIMS) permit.',
        shortSummary='Nepal is an awe-inspiring Himalayan wonderland nestled on the roof of the world, celebrated as the home of Mount Everest and eight of the world\'s ten highest peaks, the sacred birthplace of Gautama Buddha at Lumbini, ancient Newar pagoda architecture, and the legendary warmth and courage of the Nepali people.'
